For one traversal of a container, an O(n) sweep over 874 records costs roughly 2 steps per item. About how many operations occur altogether?

The loop under study is:

```cpp
int total = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 874; ++i) {
    total += 2;
}
```

What total is reported?

In an indexed lookup loop, an O(n) sweep over 693 records costs some 6 steps for each. What is the total?

The loop under study is:

```cpp
int total = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < 693; ++i) {
    total += 6;
}
```

What total is reported?
